module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FinitePresentationChartSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.InvertibleQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasicoherentCartesianOnAffineCharts
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ZeroSchemeQuasicoherentIdeal
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DualBaseChangeIdeal

/-!
# The sections of an invertible module over an affine étale chart

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B`, and let `ℒ` be
an invertible `𝒪_X`-module on the small étale site of `X`, invertible in the sense of Stacks
01CS.  This module records what invertibility gives about the sections of `ℒ` over the *affine*
étale charts of `X`, and the one consequence for the evaluation ideal of Stacks 0845 that
follows from it with no further input.

Everything here is unconditional.  That is worth saying, because the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ZeroSchemeQuasicoherentIdeal.lean` record the first
statement below — that an invertible module is cartesian on affine charts — as unavailable,
citing Descent, Proposition 03DX(2).  That proposition *is* available, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`, so the note is
stale; see the implementation notes.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isInvertible`: an invertible
  `𝒪_X`-module is cartesian on affine charts.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentationOnSite_of_isInvertible`: an invertible
  `𝒪_X`-module is of finite presentation on the small étale site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.module_finitePresentation_sections_of_isInvertible`: the sections of
  an invertible `𝒪_X`-module over an affine étale chart are a finitely presented module over the
  ring of regular functions on that chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.sectionEvaluationSubmodule_obj_eq_of_isInvertible`: the family of
  ideals generated by the evaluation ideals of a global section of an invertible module has the
  evaluation ideal itself as its value over every affine étale chart.

## Implementation notes

The three hypotheses that the chart-section results of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/FinitePresentationChartSections.lean` take — cartesian on
affine charts, finite type on the site, finite presentation on the site — are all supplied here
by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isInvertible` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isInvertible`, which route through
Stacks 0B8Q for the small étale site: an invertible module is finite locally free of rank one
because that site is locally ringed, hence of finite presentation, hence quasi-coherent.

Invertibility is spelled with `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible` at the structure
presheaf `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structureCommRings`.  That is definitionally the spelling
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsInvertibleSheaf` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Chow/EffectiveCartierIntersection.lean` uses, whose
structure presheaf is written `(smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).O.obj`, so a hypothesis in
either shape feeds the results below directly.

### On the stale note

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ZeroSchemeQuasicoherentIdeal.lean` names two obstructions
to identifying the defining ideal of the zero scheme of Stacks 0845 with the evaluation ideal.
The first — that the chartwise evaluation ideals are not known stable under restriction, for
want of Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) — is removed by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isInvertible` below, 03DX(2) being
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`.  The second
obstruction, that the *sheaf* of ideals generated by the chartwise family is not known to have
the evaluation ideals as its affine values, is not addressed here: this module computes the
value of the generated *family*
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.sectionEvaluationSubmodule`), not of the sheaf
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.sectionEvaluationIdeal` it generates.  Nothing here claims any part of
Stacks 0845 or 0846, and no declaration below carries either tag.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0845](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0845)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8Q)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **An invertible `𝒪_X`-module is cartesian on affine charts.**  It is quasi-coherent by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isInvertible`, and a quasi-coherent module is
cartesian on affine charts by Descent, Proposition 03DX(2). -/
theorem isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isInvertible (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (L : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structureCommRings B S hS X)
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS X).property L) :
    IsCartesianOnAffineCharts L :=
  isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS X.1 X.2 L
    (isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isInvertible B S hS X L hL)

/-- **An invertible `𝒪_X`-module is of finite presentation on the small étale site.**  It is
finite locally free of rank one by Stacks 0B8Q, and a finite locally free module is of finite
presentation. -/
theorem isFinitePresentationOnSite_of_isInvertible (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (L : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structureCommRings B S hS X)
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS X).property L) :
    SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentationOnSite L :=
  SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite
    (isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isInvertible B S hS X L hL).isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite

/-- **The sections of an invertible `𝒪_X`-module over an affine étale chart form a finitely
presented module over the ring of regular functions on that chart.** -/
theorem module_finitePresentation_sections_of_isInvertible (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (L : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structureCommRings B S hS X)
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS X).property L)
    (W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hW : IsAffine
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W)) :
    Module.FinitePresentation (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 W) (L.val.obj (op W)) :=
  module_finitePresentation_sections_of_isCartesian_of_isFinitePresentationOnSite L
    (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isInvertible B S hS X L hL)
    (isFinitePresentationOnSite_of_isInvertible B S hS X L hL) W hW

/-- **For a global section of an invertible `𝒪_X`-module, the family of ideals generated by the
evaluation ideals of the affine charts has the evaluation ideal as its value over every affine
étale chart.**

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.sectionEvaluationSubmodule_obj_eq_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts`
with its hypothesis discharged.  It is a statement about the generated *family*, not about the
sheaf of ideals that family generates, and so is not yet the defining ideal of the zero scheme
of Stacks 0845. -/
theorem sectionEvaluationSubmodule_obj_eq_of_isInvertible (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (L : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) (s : L.sections)
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structureCommRings B S hS X)
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS X).property L)
    (V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hV : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toSchemes B S hS X.1).obj V).1) :
    (sectionEvaluationSubmodule B S hS X L s).obj (op V) =
      sectionEvaluationIdealAt B S hS X L s V :=
  sectionEvaluationSubmodule_obj_eq_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts B S hS X L s
    (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isInvertible B S hS X L hL) V hV


/-- **For a global section of an invertible `𝒪_X`-module, the evaluation ideal over the smaller of
two affine étale charts is *generated* by the restrictions from the larger one.**

The containment in the other direction is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.sectionEvaluationIdealAt_map_le_of_bijective_sectionsBaseChange`, so
together with this the two ideals correspond exactly under restriction.

A functional `l'` on `L(V)` is read, through the base change comparison, as a `𝒪_X(V)`-linear
functional on `𝒪_X(V) ⊗ L(U)`; it evaluates at `1 ⊗ s|_U` inside the extension of the evaluation
ideal of `U` by `Module.FinitePresentation.liftBaseChange_mem_ideal_map_span_dual`, whose two
hypotheses are flatness of the chart restriction between affine charts and finite presentation of
`L(U)`. The first is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_chartRestrict_of_isAffine` and the second is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.module_finitePresentation_sections_of_isInvertible` above; no local
triviality of `L` is used. -/
theorem sectionEvaluationIdealAt_le_map_of_isInvertible (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (L : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) (s : L.sections)
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structureCommRings B S hS X)
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS X).property L)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (f : V ⟶ U)
    (hU : IsAffine
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U))
    (hV : IsAffine
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V)) :
    sectionEvaluationIdealAt B S hS X L s V ≤
      Ideal.map (chartRestrict (hF := X.2) f) (sectionEvaluationIdealAt B S hS X L s U) := by
  classical
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := X.2) f
  let _ := chartSectionsModule L f
  have _ := chartSections_isScalarTower L f
  have hflat : Module.Flat (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 U) (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 V) :=
    flat_chartRestrict_of_isAffine f hU hV
  have hfp : Module.FinitePresentation (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 U) (L.val.obj (op U)) :=
    module_finitePresentation_sections_of_isInvertible B S hS X L hL U hU
  let e := LinearEquiv.ofBijective (sectionsBaseChange L f)
    (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isInvertible B S hS X L hL U V hU hV f)
  refine Ideal.span_le.2 (Set.range_subset_iff.2 fun l' => ?_)
  have hone : e (TensorProduct.tmul (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 U)
      (1 : chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 V) (s.eval (op U))) = s.eval (op V) :=
    (chartBaseChange_one_tmul L f (s.eval (op U))).trans
      (PresheafOfModules.sections_property s f.op)
  have hmem := Module.FinitePresentation.liftBaseChange_mem_ideal_map_span_dual
    (A := chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 U) (T := chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 V)
    (M := (L.val.obj (op U) : Type u)) (s.eval (op U)) (l' ∘ₗ e.toLinearMap)
  rwa [show (l' ∘ₗ e.toLinearMap) (TensorProduct.tmul (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 U)
      (1 : chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 V) (s.eval (op U))) = l' (s.eval (op V)) from
    congrArg l' hone] at hmem

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
